accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final type  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  29 removed_month 93 accessioned on  29 removed_month 93 at 11 57 clinical data  45 year old female with extensive ductal carcinoma in situ and positive margins in previous biopsy  now presents for a mastectomy  tram reconstruction and left breast reduction                                                                                      final diagnosis     breasts and axillary contents  right   modified radical mastectomy  focal residual ductal carcinoma in situ  with pagetoid spread  lobular carcinoma in situ  see note  breast  left  1   partial excisions  infiltrating ductal carcinoma  grade removed_date intraductal carcinoma  comedo type with pagetoid spread  breast  left  2   partial excisions  infiltrating ductal carcinoma  grade removed_date intraductal carcinoma  comedo type  note  14  right axillary  lymph nodes are negative for tumor  blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not identified  diagnosis by  g  richard dickersin  m d  signed on  10 removed_month 93 at 13 14                                                                                     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     results of staining of fixed tissue for hormone receptor proteins breast  left   the tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  11 removed_month 93 at 11 15 gross description  received fresh  labeled  right breast and axillary contents   is a 750 gram  modified radical mastectomy with axillary tail  the breast measures 15 x 15 x 4cm with an axillary tail of 8 x 5 x 1cm  the irregularly shaped skin surface is 14 x 8cm and is grossly unremarkable  the nipple is likewise grossly unremarkable  14 lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail  ranging in size from 2 to 5mm  a 3cm well healed linear scar is present lateral and inferiorly from the nipple  2cm from the medial resection margin  1cm posterior from the skin and 1cm anterior from the deep resection margin is white  firm  fibrous nodular tissue  approximately  3 x 2 x 2cm  in the center of the specimen posterior and slightly superior to the scar is firm  microcystic breast parenchyma  multiple cysts are present  ranging in size up to 1cm in average dimension  the smaller cysts are 2 to 4mm in diameter  posterior and lateral to the scar is a large cystic cavity  3 x 3 x 3cm and is lined by smooth  shiny tissue  surrounding the cavity is dense  firm  white tissue with multiple microcysts  ranging in size from 5 to 10mm in average diameter  section code  a  lateral resection margin  b  inferior resection margin  c  posterior medial resection margin  